{
  "id": "DrugBank_DB11698 - MONDO_5015",
  "verbalization": "Ipragliflozin is associated with Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus through a series of indications that link it to other drugs known to affect glucose metabolism. The evidence suggests that Ipragliflozin may be repurposed for the treatment of diabetes by influencing pathways that are also targeted by other drugs like Voglibose, Nateglinide, and Vildagliptin. These drugs are typically used in the management of diabetes by modulating various metabolic processes, including insulin secretion and glucose regulation. The integration of these indications implies that Ipragliflozin may exert a similar effect, potentially through mechanisms that involve the inhibition of sodium-glucose cotransporter 2 (SGLT2), which is a key target in the treatment of Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus. The cumulative evidence supports the hypothesis that Ipragliflozin could be a viable candidate for repurposing in the management of diabetes, provided further mechanistic validation is conducted to confirm its therapeutic effects and safety profile.",
